const MAIN = '/Users/m1/marvin'
const BASE = `Repository ${MAIN}, branch codex/mos-aster-racing-city. We are porting the macOS game apps/simulator-macos (Swift, SceneKit, AppKit, AVFoundation) to Godot 4.7 .NET (C#) in apps/simulator-godot. Already done and committed: src/Core (C# port of SimulationCore, byte-identical to Swift, namespace Marvin.Core) and scripts/SceneKit (a SceneKit/AppKit/Metal/Dispatch FACADE over Godot with Swift-identical type and member names, calibrated against real SceneKit renders; global usings expose it everywhere).

READ apps/simulator-godot/PORTING.md IN FULL FIRST, especially "Translation rules", "SceneKit facade" (spelling table, shader composer, shader modifier translation guide, calibration, known deviations) and "Agent rules". Port with the facade: the C# should read almost line for line like the Swift. Keep every name verbatim. Translate each MSL shader modifier into Godot shading language following the guide. Do not simplify behaviour, skip features, or leave TODO stubs in your own files. If the facade lacks something you need, ADD it to the facade (scripts/SceneKit) in a general, SceneKit-faithful way and note it in your report (other streams edit the facade in parallel, so keep facade edits small and additive).

WORKTREE: you work in an ISOLATED GIT WORKTREE (if you are the first stage of a stream, it was just created for you - it is your current repo; if a previous stage's worktree path is given, cd there and work only there). Inside it, first run apps/simulator-godot/tools/sync-assets.py and apps/simulator-godot/tools/godot --headless --import (bounded with gtimeout). Never touch ${MAIN} directly except READING reference captures under ${MAIN}/apps/simulator-godot/reference/mac/ (gitignored macOS captures: smoke/, town/, character/, binary-sky/, sandstorm/, menu/, entrance/, dune-contact/ - PNG/JSON written by the macOS smoke modes) and reading the macOS sources. You may run the macOS game binary '${MAIN}/apps/simulator-macos/.build/Marvin Simulator.app/Contents/MacOS/MarvinSimulator' with its smoke flags to produce MORE reference captures into a temp dir under /private/tmp/claude-501/. Never modify apps/simulator-macos.

FILES: Godot-side ports go in apps/simulator-godot/scripts/<Area>/<SwiftFileName>.cs (namespace Marvin). Shaders may be inline strings like the Swift (preferred, mirrors the source) or .gdshader files. If you need a type owned by ANOTHER stream that does not exist yet (e.g. TownWorld when porting DirtWorld, Robot when porting MainMenu), create a MINIMAL stub ONLY in apps/simulator-godot/scripts/_stubs/<your-stream>.cs with the same name/namespace and just the members you call; the orchestrator deletes all stubs when merging. Never put stubs elsewhere.

MODES: add command-line modes with [GameMode("--flag")] on a static Run(string dir, SceneTree tree) method (see scripts/GameModes.cs) in your own files - never edit scripts/Main.cs. Mirror the macOS flag names, camera setups, states and OUTPUT FILE NAMES so captures compare 1:1. Run them with: apps/simulator-godot/tools/godot -- --flag DIR (bounded with gtimeout).

Shell quirks: 'cat'/'ls' are aliased to missing tools - use 'command cat', 'command ls' or the Read tool. Build with apps/simulator-godot/tools/build (must end with 0 errors). At the END of your stage, COMMIT in the worktree (git add apps/simulator-godot; git commit -m "<what you did>"; no push). Report honestly what works, what differs from the macOS captures, and what is missing.`

